Changelog: 25-11-2026 23:40:24

Added. The dashboard has a tile for Nexus Marketing for PS5, which it finds in dev/marketing. The window's
info and the README name it.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 20:47:37

Added. Portal video tour has the option A voice reads the captions out, with Nexus TTS's speech engine. It is checked
at first. Unchecked, the tour is recorded with --no-voice. The dialog and the tile say the tour runs about three minutes
and takes a few minutes to record.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 15:46:27

Breaking. Nexus Dashboard is now called Nexus Dashboard for PS5. Its ID is now nexus-dashboard-ps5 instead of
nexus-dashboard, which both suites shared. That ID names the launcher in ~/.local/bin, the menu entry, the Desktop
icon, the settings folder, the log folder and the check for an open window. Both suites' dashboards can now be
installed and opened side by side. Before, the one installed last replaced the other, and opening one closed the
other. install.sh removes the old nexus-dashboard launcher, menu entry and Desktop icon when that launcher starts
this checkout.

